dingClientRect()</code>, developers needed m=E1=BB=99t way =C4=91=E1=BB=83 =
get element coordinates relative to their positioning context. <code class=
=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 white=
space-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">offsetLeft</code>=
 v=C3=A0 <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 t=
ext-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem=
]">offsetTop</code> were designed =C4=91=E1=BB=83 provide this information =
efficiently.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">These properties answer the ques=
tion: "Where is this element relative to its offsetParent's upper-left corn=
er?"</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">=F0=9F=94=AC <strong>B=E1=BA=A3n=
 Ch=E1=BA=A5t &amp; Mechanism:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Browser calculates offsetLeft/of=
fsetTop during layout phase b=E1=BA=B1ng c=C3=A1ch:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Determine offsetParent<=
/strong>: Find reference element</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Calculate border box</s=
trong>: Include element's content + padding + border</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Measure distance</stron=
g>: From offsetParent's content edge to element's border edge</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Account for scrolling</=
strong>: offsetParent's scroll position doesn't affect these values</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Critical Insight</strong=
>: offsetLeft/offsetTop measure t=E1=BB=9Bi element's border edge, not cont=
ent edge.</p>
